        </aside>

        <!-- FAQ -->
        <section id="faq" class="ed-faq scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
          <details open>
            <summary><h3>What treadmills does Sam’s Club sell?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Mainly NordicTrack and ProForm, both made by iFIT. Sam’s Club’s own pages have listed the NordicTrack Commercial Series 1250, 1750 and 2450, the Commercial LE, X16, EXP Series 7i and T Series models, and the ProForm Carbon TLS, Carbon TLX and Carbon Pro 9000. Stock and prices change, and some prices are shown only to members.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Does Sam’s Club sell the NordicTrack Commercial 1750?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Sam’s Club has listed it as the NordicTrack Commercial Series 1750, with a members-only price. Check that the listing describes the current model, with a 22 by 60-inch belt, a 400 lb rating and a 16-inch pivoting screen.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>What is the NordicTrack Commercial LE?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              A retailer model sold at Sam’s Club, Abt, Best Buy and Nebraska Furniture Mart but not on NordicTrack’s own US range. It has a -3% to 12% grade range, 12 mph and a 7-inch display instead of a touchscreen. Retailers disagree on its motor rating, so confirm it with NordicTrack before buying.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>What is Sam’s Club’s return policy on treadmills?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Sam’s Club’s returns page lets most items be returned at any time, with 90 days for electronics and major appliances. Treadmills are not named, so check the return terms on the treadmill’s product page or ask Member Services. Items bought in a club cannot be shipped back, and online purchases can generally go to any US club.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Do you need a membership to buy a treadmill at Sam’s Club?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Generally yes, and several treadmill prices are shown only to signed-in members. The Club membership is $60 a year and Plus $120 since May 2026. Sam’s membership guarantee offers a refund of the current year’s fee if you are unsatisfied.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Is Sam’s Club or Costco better for a treadmill?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Neither is consistently cheaper. Both have listed the NordicTrack Commercial 1750, both have broad return policies with electronics exceptions, and Costco’s basic membership costs $65 against Sam’s $60. If you already belong to one, check that one first and compare the delivered price on the same day.
            </p>
          </details>
        </section>

        <!-- Why trust us -->
        <section id="why-trust-us" class="ed-trust not-prose">
          <h2>Why trust Treadmill Reviews USA?</h2>
          <p>
            Every recommendation is checked against the numbers that matter for a treadmill: the maker's own
            listing and manual, at least one independent source, the warranty terms and the CPSC recall
            database. Where sources disagree we say so rather than pick a number, we say plainly when a
            machine has not been tested hands-on, and we never accept payment for a placement. <a href="/editorial-standards/">Read our review process.</a>
          </p>
